invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_mont_square adds nothing at a row's offset k, where a_i
  times the top bit of a_{k-1} belongs, so every square of a number whose
  top word has its top bit set comes out short. bin/rsa_equiv_test holds
  the square to the multiplication of the number by itself, and squares
  n - 1 and the top bit alone under moduli with the top bit set.

--- old
            ct_u128 sum = (ct_u128)(*a_word & mask_of_bit(*d_top)) + t[k] + ab_carry;
--- new
            ct_u128 sum = (ct_u128)(*a_word & mask_of_bit(*d_top) & 0) + t[k] + ab_carry;
